# Alembic migrations for Plenvo

## Commands (run from `backend/`)

```bash
# Apply migrations
python -m alembic upgrade head

# Autogenerate a new migration after model changes
python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe_change"

# Mark DB as up-to-date without running (existing synced DBs)
python -m alembic stamp head
```

Database URL comes from `Settings.database_url` (`.env` / environment), not from `alembic.ini`.

App startup (`init_db`) only runs non-destructive `create_all` for missing tables.
Do **not** use `drop_all` for schema changes — add Alembic migrations instead.
